(125, 'Retatrutide 5mg', 'Reta-05', '10020', '2482951-73-7', 'LY3437943; Retatrutide Peptide', NULL, '5 mg', 'C215H343N59O64', 'Slightly soluble in water and acetic acid; insoluble in ethanol', 'Powder: –20°C (3 yrs); 4°C (2 yrs); 15°C (3 mo); In solvent: –80°C (6 mo); –20°C (1 mo); 10°C (1 wk)', 'Ambient temperature shipping', 'White to off-white lyophilized powder', '≥99.4%', '682146', 'I noticed that different peptides have different CAS numbers, synonyms, and formulas. But when it comes to one specific peptide that is available in multiple doses—like Retatrutide (5mg, 10mg, 20mg, 30mg)—the CAS number, synonyms, and formula remain the same. This is because Retatrutide is a single peptide, and only the dose varies. The molecular identity does not change, only the amount in the vial.', '2025-04-01', '2027-04-01', '2025-09-09 22:00:10'),
